Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||07-11-2001||04:34 PM||||I just got it about 40 min ago ..and I'm slap happy. Brian labeled each wire , should be easy to install. Just reading the instructions for the 50th time. <P>I'm excited to try it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Here mustang mustang mustang<P>I got the plate made that mounts under the ashtray door. 1 switch to open the bottle , the other just says "Go baby go"<P>haha<P>JM<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000008||NOS3800||07-11-2001||08:37 PM||||Some of the information you seek can be found on the webpage. I am HAPPY with the ACE kit and their customer service is top notch. I got my wiring and speedo conversion back from them in a month. The installation to the 88 cradle was done with GM mounts(with shaved parts numbers). There was only need to gain some clearance on the driver side of cradle so the tranny wouldn't rub. This was done my torching the length and folding it in and then reweld.If I waited till I had everything together, the conversion could have been done in one weekend. The only problem I had was the price. At the time the kit cost 1300. BUT it went SOOOOO smoothly, I did it myself( I am a autobody tech). My brother did the SC install using Chris West components and some of his own fabricated mounts. His is an 85. But he used a wiring harness guy that screwed him for 8 months!! He had to rewire the thing when he got it back.<BR>My NOS kit is a ZEX dry kit set at 75 HP. I LOVE IT!!!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
